Phase 2.4: The Social Graph, System Maturity & Data Insights (Master Spec)
Project: Highland Events Hub Current State: Post-Phase 2.3 Objective: Transform into a community platform with robust social features, secure auth, and a powerful Analytics Engine.

📅 Sprint 1: Auth, Identity & Profiles
Goal: Transition from Email-based identity to Username-based identity and secure the platform.

1. Database Schema Updates (users or profiles table)
Add Columns:

username (Text, Unique, Nullable initially).

display_name (Text, Nullable).

trust_level (Integer, Default: 0).

is_admin (Boolean, Default: false) - Ensure this exists for the new moderation logic.

2. The "Username Migration" (Blocker Logic)
Scenario: Existing users have no username. New users must pick one.

Sign-Up Flow: Update the Registration Form to add a mandatory "Username" field. Check uniqueness before submit.

Existing User Flow (The Blocker):

Logic: On every page load (or inside the Layout wrapper), check: if (user && !user.username).

Action: If true, trigger a Full Screen Modal (cannot be closed).

Modal Content: "Choose your Username to continue." Input field + Submit button.

Backend: Update the record. Once set, the modal disappears.

3. Google Login Integration
Implementation: Add "Continue with Google" button to Login/Signup forms.

Library: Use your existing Auth provider's Google integration (or standard OAuth2).

Logic:

If the Google email matches an existing account, link them.

If new, create account and trigger the Username Blocker modal immediately after redirect.

📅 Sprint 2: The Social Layer (Groups & Following)
Goal: Connect users to Organizers and Venues.

1. The "Follow" System
Database Table: follows

id (Primary Key)

follower_id (User ID, Foreign Key)

target_id (UUID - Linked to Venue OR Organizer)

target_type (String/Enum: 'venue' or 'group')

created_at (Timestamp)

Constraint: Unique composite key on [follower_id, target_id] (User can't follow same thing twice).

UI Components:

Profile Header (Venue & Group Pages): Add a "Follow" toggle button.

State: If row exists in follows table -> "Following" (Active style). Else -> "Follow" (Outline style).

Dashboard ("My Feed" Tab):

Query: Fetch Events where (venue_id IN user_followed_venue_ids) OR (organizer_id IN user_followed_group_ids).

Sort: Chronological (Newest created or Upcoming).

2. Group Management (Invite Links)
Database Table: group_members

group_id (Foreign Key)

user_id (Foreign Key)

role (String: 'owner', 'editor')

Database Table: group_invites

token (String, Unique, Index)

group_id (Foreign Key)

created_at (Timestamp)

expires_at (Timestamp - e.g., 7 days)

UI & Logic:

Owner Dashboard: "Generate Invite Link" button.

Action: Creates a row in group_invites and returns URL: .../join/group/[token].

The "Join" Page (/join/group/[token]):

On load, validate token (check if exists and not expired).

If valid: Show "Join [Group Name]?" button.

On Click: Add user to group_members (Role: 'editor'), delete the invite token, redirect to Group Dashboard.

📅 Sprint 3: Admin & Moderation Overhaul
Goal: Streamline operations and organize the chaos.

1. Moderation Logic Upgrade (The "Trust" System)
Backend "Create Event" Logic:

Current: All events -> Pending.

New:

JavaScript

if (user.is_admin || user.trust_level > 0) {
    status = 'approved';
} else {
    status = 'pending';
}
"Approve Series" Action:

In the Admin Queue, when clicking "Approve" on an event with a parent_event_id:

Action: Update status = 'approved' for ALL events where parent_event_id matches the target. (Bulk update).

2. Admin Dashboard Redesign
Layout: Replace the 4 big cards with a single "Platform Health" panel.

Columns: Users (Total/New), Events (Active/Pending), Venues.

Navigation: Update Sidebar to use Collapsible Categories:

Manage: Events, Venues, Groups, Users.

System: Categories, Tags, Moderation.

Data: Analytics (Placeholder).

📅 Sprint 4: The Analytics Engine (Data Capture)
Goal: Capture raw intent and conversion data.

1. Database Table: analytics_events
Columns:

id (PK)

timestamp (DateTime, Default: Now)

user_id (Nullable - for logged in users)

visitor_id (String - Anonymous session ID/Cookie)

event_type (String: 'page_view', 'click_ticket', 'save_event', 'search_query', 'click_website')

target_id (UUID, Nullable - The Event/Venue ID being viewed)

meta_data (JSON/Text - e.g., Search terms, Referrer URL)

2. The Capture Mechanism (Hook/Service)
Component: Create a global AnalyticsTracker or Hook.

Triggers:

Page Load: Fire page_view (Path: URL).

Search Bar: When user hits "Search" (not typing), fire search_query (Term: "Jazz").

Ticket Button: On Click, fire click_ticket.

Save Button: On Click, fire save_event.

Performance Note: These writes should be "fire and forget" (don't await the promise in the UI).

📅 Sprint 5: Insights & Polish
Goal: Visualize the data and clean up the frontend.

1. The Insights Dashboard (Admin)
View: Create /admin/insights.

Widget A (Content Gaps): Query analytics_events for event_type = 'search_query'. Group by term, count frequency. Display Top 10.

Widget B (Conversion): Calculate % of page_view events that result in click_ticket for the last 30 days.

2. Event Owner Stats (User Dashboard)
View: On "My Events" or "Event Details" for the owner.

Data: Count rows in analytics_events where target_id matches this event.

Display: Simple cards: "Total Views: 120", "Ticket Clicks: 5", "Saves: 12".

3. Homepage "Popular" Section
Logic: Query analytics_events:

Filter: event_type = 'page_view', timestamp > (Now - 7 Days).

Group By: target_id.

Order By: Count Descending.

Limit: 10.

UI: Render these events in a new "Trending Now" strip on the homepage.

🚫 Critical Constraints
Tech Stack Agnostic: Use generic DB logic. Code must work with the existing ORM/Query builder (e.g., Prisma, Drizzle, TypeORM, or raw SQL).

Past Events: Update the main getEvents query (Public) to strictly filter out dates before Today (date >= NOW()).

Analytics: Do not block the UI waiting for analytics to save.